\n+.ruff_cache/\r\n.gitignore:19: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\n.gitignore:20: trailing whitespace.\n+# Runtime and local work output\r\n.gitignore:21: trailing whitespace.\n+/runs/\r\n.gitignore:22: trailing whitespace.\n+/scratch/\r\n.gitignore:23: trailing whitespace.\n+/.firm/\r\n.gitignore:24: trailing whitespace.\n+/packs/\r\n.gitignore:25: trailing whitespace.\n+/boards/\r\n.gitignore:26: trailing whitespace.\n+/firmware/\r\n.gitignore:27: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\n.gitignore:28: trailing whitespace.\n+# OS and editor metadata\r\n.gitignore:29: trailing whitespace.\n+.DS_Store\r\n.gitignore:30: trailing whitespace.\n+*.swp\r\n.gitignore:31: trailing whitespace.\n+.idea/\r\n.gitignore:32: trailing whitespace.\n+.vscode/\r\n.gitignore:33: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\n.gitignore:34: trailing whitespace.\n+# uv.lock and .python-version are intentionally tracked.\r\n.python-version:1: trailing whitespace.\n+3.12\r\nREADME.md:1: trailing whitespace.\n+# BYO Server Firmware Workflow\r\nREADME.md:2: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\nREADME.md:3: trailing whitespace.\n+BYO Server is a guarded local MCP server for embedded-board setup, debugging, serial I/O,\r\nREADME.md:4: trailing whitespace.\n+deployment, and recovery through pyOCD.\r\nREADME.md:5: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\nREADME.md:6: trailing whitespace.\n+## Install and connect\r\nREADME.md:7: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\nREADME.md:8: trailing whitespace.\n+Install the locked environment from the checkout:\r\nREADME.md:9: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\nREADME.md:10: trailing whitespace.\n+```text\r\nREADME.md:11: trailing whitespace.\n+uv sync --locked\r\nREADME.md:12: trailing whitespace.\n+```\r\nREADME.md:13: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\nREADME.md:14: trailing whitespace.\n+Register this stdio command in any MCP-compatible client:\r\nREADME.md:15: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\nREADME.md:16: trailing whitespace.\n+```text\r\nREADME.md:17: trailing whitespace.\n+uv run --project <absolute-path-to-BYO-Server> --locked pyocd-debug-mcp\r\nREADME.md:18: trailing whitespace.\n+```\r\nREADME.md:19: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\nREADME.md:20: trailing whitespace.\n+For example:\r\nREADME.md:21: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\nREADME.md:22: trailing whitespace.\n+```text\r\nREADME.md:23: trailing whitespace.\n+codex mcp add byo-firmware -- uv run --project C:\\Users\\Jason\\Documents\\Jason\\FirmCLI_Tester\\BYO-Firmware-MCP --locked pyocd-debug-mcp\r\nREADME.md:24: trailing whitespace.\n+```\r\nREADME.md:25: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\nREADME.md:26: trailing whitespace.\n+-> For the user Jason, using codex, where the server is stored at \\FirmCLI_Tester\\BYO-Firmware-MCP, this is the registration command.\r\nREADME.md:27: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\nREADME.md:28: trailing whitespace.\n+The server is client-neutral and never launches a client workflow or silently connects to hardware. See\r\nREADME.md:29: trailing whitespace.\n+[SERVER_GUIDE.md](SERVER_GUIDE.md) for the full setup and tool workflow.\r\nREADME.md:30: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\nREADME.md:31: trailing whitespace.\n+## Firmware MCP capabilities\r\nREADME.md:32: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\nREADME.md:33: trailing whitespace.\n+The server provides a guarded board-development surface:\r\nREADME.md:34: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\nREADME.md:35: trailing whitespace.\n+- **Board readiness:** discover connections, route familiar board names to validation or setup,\r\nREADME.md:36: trailing whitespace.\n+  establish board profiles, validate live hardware, and report readiness.\r\nREADME.md:37: trailing whitespace.\n+- **Debug and inspection:** inspect board, CPU, execution, symbol, and bounded-memory state;\r\nREADME.md:38: trailing whitespace.\n+  control breakpoints, stepping, reset/run, and other bounded diagnostic actions.\r\nREADME.md:39: trailing whitespace.\n+- **Serial evidence:** capture UART output and run controlled serial exchanges for declared tests\r\nREADME.md:40: trailing whitespace.\n+  or diagnosis.\r\nREADME.md:41: trailing whitespace.\n+- **Firmware deployment:** bind the selected build output in a flash plan, verify it against the\r\nREADME.md:42: trailing whitespace.\n+  reviewed stable map at execution time, and flash the approved application. A successful flash\r\nREADME.md:43: trailing whitespace.\n+  is deployment evidence, not proof of behavior.\r\nREADME.md:44: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\nREADME.md:45: trailing whitespace.\n+`find_symbol`, `read_memory_symbol`, and symbol-backed `write_memory` accept the current project's\r\nREADME.md:46: trailing whitespace.\n+ELF explicitly. Pass `elf_artifact` after a server restart; within one uninterrupted Server Run, a\r\nREADME.md:47: trailing whitespace.\n+successful application flash also creates a temporary convenience binding. The server never swaps\r\nREADME.md:48: trailing whitespace.\n+in implicit checkout firmware as another project's symbol table, and symbol addresses remain\r\nREADME.md:49: trailing whitespace.\n+subject to the board's memory-map containment policy.\r\nREADME.md:50: trailing whitespace.\n+- **Guarded mutation and recovery:** writes, execution changes, bootloader work, and recovery\r\nREADME.md:51: trailing whitespace.\n+  require the current board gate, the exact `*-plan` action, and any required human permission.\r\nREADME.md:52: trailing whitespace.\n+- **Per-board safety:** validation, plans, permissions, budgets, and results never transfer between\r\nREADME.md:53: trailing whitespace.\n+  connections. Disconnects and new server runs require validation; stable-map problems use the\r\nREADME.md:54: trailing whitespace.\n+  server's refresh path.\r\nREADME.md:55: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\nREADME.md:56: trailing whitespace.\n+Always follow live MCP guidance. Visibility is not authorization: guarded actions use an all-null\r\nREADME.md:57: trailing whitespace.\n+`*-plan` guidance call, the returned populated plan submission, then the paired action.\r\nREADME.md:58: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\nREADME.md:59: trailing whitespace.\n+### Portable native-build artifacts\r\nREADME.md:60: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\nREADME.md:61: trailing whitespace.\n+The server does not require a particular IDE or build system. Build with the project's native\r\nREADME.md:62: trailing whitespace.\n+tooling, then optionally normalize its explicit outputs with the small collector:\r\nREADME.md:63: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\nREADME.md:64: trailing whitespace.\n+```text\r\nREADME.md:65: trailing whitespace.\n+uv run --locked python -m pyocd_debug_mcp.artifact_collector \\\r\nREADME.md:66: trailing whitespace.\n+  --output-dir build/collected --producer native-project-build \\\r\nREADME.md:67: trailing whitespace.\n+  --elf path/to/application.elf --hex path/to/application.hex \\\r\nREADME.md:68: trailing whitespace.\n+  --map path/to/application.map --expect elf --expect map\r\nREADME.md:69: trailing whitespace.\n+```\r\nREADME.md:70: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\nREADME.md:71: trailing whitespace.\n+The collector copies explicitly typed ELF, HEX, BIN, and linker-map files byte-for-byte into\r\nREADME.md:72: trailing whitespace.\n+canonical `firmware.*` names and records portable SHA-256 provenance in `build-manifest.json`. It\r\nREADME.md:73: trailing whitespace.\n+does not run a build, discover memory permissions, access hardware, or authorize flashing. Use the\r\nREADME.md:74: trailing whitespace.\n+canonical output in the matching flash plan; safety refresh accepts no build artifacts, and a raw\r\nREADME.md:75: trailing whitespace.\n+BIN has no trusted load address.\r\nREADME.md:76: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\nREADME.md:77: trailing whitespace.\n+MCP clients can use the same behavior through the always-visible\r\nREADME.md:78: trailing whitespace.\n+`collect_build_artifacts` tool. Its indexed description gives the exact call contract and its\r\nREADME.md:79: trailing whitespace.\n+response returns canonical paths plus the flash-plan handoff. For guarded firmware, normally\r\nREADME.md:80: trailing whitespace.\n+supply the coherent ELF and linker map with `expected_roles=[\"elf\", \"map\"]`. The standalone CLI\r\nREADME.md:81: trailing whitespace.\n+remains useful to developers and terminal-driven workflows outside an MCP session.\r\nREADME.md:82: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\nREADME.md:83: trailing whitespace.\n+For a server-directed build, inspect the project's own build files and use the\r\nREADME.md:84: trailing whitespace.\n+`pyocd_debug_mcp.native_build` argv template from `get_setup_status.build_guidance`. Put the exact\r\nREADME.md:85: trailing whitespace.\n+native build argv after `--`; the helper runs it directly without a shell and reports its cwd,\r\nREADME.md:86: trailing whitespace.\n+network policy, exit code, ELF/HEX format checks, and map provenance. It does not invent universal\r\nREADME.md:90: trailing whitespace.\n+`--timeout-seconds`, and repeatable `--artifact ROLE=PATH` declarations cover arbitrary SDKs,\r\nREADME.md:91: trailing whitespace.\n+vendor CLIs, IDE wrappers, output formats, and future build systems without a server adapter. Known\r\nREADME.md:92: trailing whitespace.\n+ELF/HEX formats receive structural checks; opaque formats are reported only as existing nonempty\r\nREADME.md:93: trailing whitespace.\n+files. Prefer a compatible installed toolchain, but acquire one normally\r\nREADME.md:94: trailing whitespace.\n+when none exists. Network access is inherited by default; `--offline` is an intentional best-effort\r\nREADME.md:95: trailing whitespace.\n+set of common-client environment guards, not an OS network sandbox or implicit policy. The server\r\nREADME.md:96: trailing whitespace.\n+does not detect or select a provider, SDK root, compiler, board target, or installation layout.\r\nREADME.md:97: trailing whitespace.\n+Every build system uses the same exact-argv path. The helper never accesses hardware or grants\r\nREADME.md:98: trailing whitespace.\n+safety authority.\r\nREADME.md:99: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\nREADME.md:100: trailing whitespace.\n+Fresh boards do not need a checked-in board YAML. Given an exact MCU ordering code and local PDF,\r\nREADME.md:101: trailing whitespace.\n+setup first replays verified local support and otherwise requests either an exact\r\nREADME.md:102: trailing whitespace.\n+installed pyOCD target or one official CMSIS-Pack. The server—not the client—replays built-in static\r\nREADME.md:103: trailing whitespace.\n+geometry or bounds and hashes the archive, proves its exact PDSC leaf, and derives the pack target.\r\nREADME.md:104: trailing whitespace.\n+It tests a non-destructive live attach before recording project-local support; a built-in target\r\nREADME.md:105: trailing whitespace.\n+with partial metadata remains usable for only the capabilities it can prove. Setup captures the\r\nREADME.md:106: trailing whitespace.\n+exact datasheet bytes as immutable source evidence and creates a\r\nREADME.md:107: trailing whitespace.\n+schema-v3 map from separate pack flash/RAM/ROM ranges and optional SVD peripheral blocks. Unknown\r\nREADME.md:108: trailing whitespace.\n+identity, erase, peripheral, deployment, or recovery facts disable only the dependent capability;\r\nREADME.md:109: trailing whitespace.\n+they are never guessed from a part name. Core-compatibility identity permits bounded read/debug and\r\nREADME.md:110: trailing whitespace.\n+guarded artifact-contained application programming; bootloader and recovery authority remain\r\nREADME.md:111: trailing whitespace.\n+separate, and setup status reports that distinction before deployment planning.\r\nREADME.md:112: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\nREADME.md:154: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\nREADME.md:155: trailing whitespace.\n+- [Server operation and recovery](SERVER_GUIDE.md)\r\nREADME.md:156: trailing whitespace.\n+- [MCP client contract](docs/client-contract.md)\r\nREADME.md:157: trailing whitespace.\n+- [Architecture and state ownership](docs/architecture.md)\r\nREADME.md:158: trailing whitespace.\n+- [Plan-tool contract](docs/plan-tool-contract.md)\r\nREADME.md:159: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:1: trailing whitespace.\n+# BYO Server Guide\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:2: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:3: trailing whitespace.\n+BYO Server is a headless local MCP server for safe embedded-board setup,\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:4: trailing whitespace.\n+debugging, serial I/O, flash, and recovery through pyOCD. It runs over stdio\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:5: trailing whitespace.\n+only. Any compatible MCP client can use it; the server, not the client, owns\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:6: trailing whitespace.\n+plans, permissions, board routing, validation, safety containment, timeouts,\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:7: trailing whitespace.\n+and cleanup.\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:8: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:9: trailing whitespace.\n+## Start the server\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:10: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:11: trailing whitespace.\n+The repository is intentionally a fresh-start distribution: it contains no board profiles, packs,\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:12: trailing whitespace.\n+reference firmware, reviewed-device catalog, or generated `.firm` state. Install the locked\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:13: trailing whitespace.\n+environment, then register the stdio command with any MCP-compatible client:\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:14: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:15: trailing whitespace.\n+```text\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:16: trailing whitespace.\n+uv sync --locked\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:17: trailing whitespace.\n+uv run --project <absolute-path-to-BYO-Server> --locked pyocd-debug-mcp\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:18: trailing whitespace.\n+```\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:19: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:20: trailing whitespace.\n+The client-specific registration wrapper varies, but the command and arguments do not. Stdout is\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:21: trailing whitespace.\n+reserved for MCP framing. Each project should set `BYO_MCP_ARTIFACT_ROOT` when it needs state outside\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:22: trailing whitespace.\n+its default project `.firm` directory. Setup creates project-local profiles and verified pack\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:23: trailing whitespace.\n+metadata only after the client supplies the user's exact part number, datasheet, and researched target\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:24: trailing whitespace.\n+or pack candidate.\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:25: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:26: trailing whitespace.\n+Generic command-line utilities are available without any bundled board data:\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:27: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:28: trailing whitespace.\n+```text\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:29: trailing whitespace.\n+uv run --locked pyocd-pack-repair --help\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:30: trailing whitespace.\n+uv run --locked pyocd-native-build --help\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:31: trailing whitespace.\n+uv run --locked pyocd-collect-artifacts --help\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:32: trailing whitespace.\n+```\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:33: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:34: trailing whitespace.\n+After setup validation, `get_setup_status` returns advisory, provider-neutral\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:35: trailing whitespace.\n+build guidance. The client inspects the project's own build metadata, resolves\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:36: trailing whitespace.\n+its actual toolchain and target, and supplies exact argv to\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:37: trailing whitespace.\n+`<server-python> -m pyocd_debug_mcp.native_build ... -- <command>`. The server\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:38: trailing whitespace.\n+does not choose an SDK, compiler, provider, or target. Compatible local tools\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:39: trailing whitespace.\n+are preferred; ordinary acquisition is allowed when none is usable. Build\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:40: trailing whitespace.\n+guidance never grants memory authority.\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:41: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:42: trailing whitespace.\n+Plan fields, budgets, and permission modes are listed in\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:43: trailing whitespace.\n+[`docs/plan-tool-contract.md`](docs/plan-tool-contract.md), which is derived\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:44: trailing whitespace.\n+from the same definitions used by the live MCP schemas. Setup resolves the\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:45: trailing whitespace.\n+current UART port from the selected stable identity and computes the datasheet\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:46: trailing whitespace.\n+SHA-256 itself; clients never need to bind a COM path or run a hash command.\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:47: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:48: trailing whitespace.\n+## Tool surface\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:49: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:50: trailing whitespace.\n+Call `initialization_handshake` first. The live `tools/list` response is the\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:51: trailing whitespace.\n+authoritative advertised surface; visibility can change after plan/setup calls.\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:52: trailing whitespace.\n+A visible tool is never proof of authorization.\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:53: trailing whitespace.\n+After a plan is accepted, dynamic clients should use its newly exposed direct\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:54: trailing whitespace.\n+action. Clients with a static function binding can use the exact returned\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:55: trailing whitespace.\n+single-child `action_batch` fallback; it follows the identical guarded dispatch\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:56: trailing whitespace.\n+path and is never permission to invent hidden calls.\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:57: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:58: trailing whitespace.\n+Always-advertised operational tools cover:\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:59: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:60: trailing whitespace.\n+- connection and inspection: profile-only `connect`, `disconnect`, `get_board_info`,\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:61: trailing whitespace.\n+  `get_state`, `read_cpu_register`, `read_execution_state`, `find_symbol`, and\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:62: trailing whitespace.\n+  `read_memory_symbol`;\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:63: trailing whitespace.\n+- ordinary execution: `halt`, `resume`, `step`, `reset_and_run`,\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:64: trailing whitespace.\n+  `remove_breakpoint`, and bounded `wait`;\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:65: trailing whitespace.\n+- setup and safety: familiar-name `setup_overview`, `load_setup_tool`,\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:66: trailing whitespace.\n+  setup-first `board_setup-plan`, strict `continue_setup`,\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:67: trailing whitespace.\n+  application/bootloader-aware `board_safety_refresh`, `board_validate`,\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:68: trailing whitespace.\n+  and the non-authoritative `get_setup_status` readiness barrier;\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:69: trailing whitespace.\n+- orchestration: `action_batch`; and\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:70: trailing whitespace.\n+- the `*-plan` tools for guarded actions.\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:71: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:72: trailing whitespace.\n+Guarded actions are registered but hidden until their exact plan unlocks them:\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:73: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:74: trailing whitespace.\n+- connection/execution: `connect_override`, `connect_under_reset`,\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:75: trailing whitespace.\n+  `reset_and_halt`, `write_cpu_register`, and `set_execution_state`;\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:76: trailing whitespace.\n+- memory/register/debug: `read_memory_address`, `write_memory`,\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:77: trailing whitespace.\n+  `register_write`, and `set_breakpoint`;\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:78: trailing whitespace.\n+- serial and flash: `read_serial`, `write_serial`, single-open\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:79: trailing whitespace.\n+  `serial_exchange`, `flash_application`, and\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:80: trailing whitespace.\n+  permission-locked `flash_bootloader`;\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:81: trailing whitespace.\n+- destructive recovery: `target_unlock`, which requires fresh one-time\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:82: trailing whitespace.\n+  approval and leaves the validation gate closed; and\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:83: trailing whitespace.\n+- setup mutation: `board_setup` and `board_fix_setup`, exposed only through\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:84: trailing whitespace.\n+  the setup loader and plan workflow.\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:85: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:86: trailing whitespace.\n+Normal `connect(board_id)` resolves only the named project profile and its\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:87: trailing whitespace.\n+profile-matched probe. It accepts no probe UID, target, external board-config,\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:88: trailing whitespace.\n+or launch-environment override. If an exceptional manual connection is truly\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:89: trailing whitespace.\n+needed, initialize `connect_override-plan` and use the hidden run-scoped\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:90: trailing whitespace.\n+`connect_override`; it never rewrites the profile. `action_batch` uses the same\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:91: trailing whitespace.\n+strict child schema and cannot smuggle those fields through normal `connect`.\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:92: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:93: trailing whitespace.\n+Memory reads are contained to the exact bytes the backend will access. Mapped\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:94: trailing whitespace.\n+RAM, flash, ROM, CPU-system, and peripheral reads remain available, including\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:95: trailing whitespace.\n+deliberately prohibited security/provisioning spans when they are authoritatively\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:96: trailing whitespace.\n+mapped. Unknown or unmapped spans and write-only peripheral reads are refused\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:97: trailing whitespace.\n+before target I/O. Every mutation remains refused for prohibited regions. This\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:98: trailing whitespace.\n+applies to both raw-address reads and symbol-resolved reads; use the named\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:99: trailing whitespace.\n+safety-setup remedy for an incomplete map, or choose a different mapped address\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:100: trailing whitespace.\n+for a write-only peripheral.\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:101: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:102: trailing whitespace.\n+After the handshake, ask the user only for familiar board names and pass them\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:103: trailing whitespace.\n+to `setup_overview`. The normalized phrase `no board` is a literal sentinel\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:104: trailing whitespace.\n+that must be passed alone, never treated as a candidate profile name. Every\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:105: trailing whitespace.\n+matching YAML routes to validation first; unknown names route to setup, and\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:106: trailing whitespace.\n+validation may return a specific repair. The response supplies bounded\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:107: trailing whitespace.\n+`load_call`, `next_call`, or plan-template objects with every server-known ID\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:108: trailing whitespace.\n+already filled. Copy those fields into MCP calls; never ask the user to invent\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:109: trailing whitespace.\n+them or to hash a datasheet. `load_setup_tool` then returns guidance only for\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:110: trailing whitespace.\n+the requested setup tool. If setup or validation returns a friendly choice,\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:111: trailing whitespace.\n+relay its prose and copy its exact `accepted_response`; do not scrape labels,\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:112: trailing whitespace.\n+invent a target, or ask the user for internal IDs.\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:113: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:114: trailing whitespace.\n+Exact schemas and status payload behavior are in\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:115: trailing whitespace.\n+[docs/client-contract.md](docs/client-contract.md) and the live MCP descriptions.\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:116: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:117: trailing whitespace.\n+## Safety model\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:118: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:119: trailing whitespace.\n+Each logical board has one live connection and one operation boundary.\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:120: trailing whitespace.\n+Same-board calls serialize while different boards can execute concurrently.\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:121: trailing whitespace.\n+Guarded requests are scoped to their run, board, session, exact parameters,\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:122: trailing whitespace.\n+plan budget, and permission.\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:123: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:124: trailing whitespace.\n+When multiple SEGGER J-Link probes are used from one server process, the server\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:125: trailing whitespace.\n+detects the selected probe provider dynamically. The first live J-Link session\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:126: trailing whitespace.\n+uses the provider's normal DLL instance; each additional simultaneous J-Link\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:127: trailing whitespace.\n+session gets an isolated temporary DLL instance, as required by pylink. Closing\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:128: trailing whitespace.\n+the normal owner releases that fast path immediately, even if isolated sessions\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:129: trailing whitespace.\n+remain live. This allocation does not depend on board names, probe serials,\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:130: trailing whitespace.\n+target types, USB locations, or host-specific library paths.\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:131: trailing whitespace.\n+If provider closure cannot be confirmed, the server keeps the affected DLL/session\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:132: trailing whitespace.\n+reservation and reports the close failure; later J-Links remain safely isolated.\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:133: trailing whitespace.\n+Restart the server after resolving the probe/USB fault to reclaim the normal fast path.\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:134: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:135: trailing whitespace.\n+Only successful `board_validate` opens the in-memory gate. Writes recheck the\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:136: trailing whitespace.\n+current aggregate safety fingerprint on every call and apply typed containment\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:137: trailing whitespace.\n+before backend mutation. Disconnect and restart clear live assignments, plans,\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:138: trailing whitespace.\n+permissions, and gates. Files under `.firm` are durable evidence only and can\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:139: trailing whitespace.\n+never restore authority.\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:140: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:141: trailing whitespace.\n+Target recovery and bootloader flash are destructive operations with stronger\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:142: trailing whitespace.\n+approval rules. Never treat conversational approval, a report, tool visibility,\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:143: trailing whitespace.\n+or a prior run as current authorization.\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:144: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:145: trailing whitespace.\n+## Build and import check\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:146: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:147: trailing whitespace.\n+The distributable package can be checked without operating hardware:\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:148: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:149: trailing whitespace.\n+```text\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:150: trailing whitespace.\n+uv build\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:151: trailing whitespace.\n+uv run --locked python -c \"import pyocd_debug_mcp; import pyocd_debug_mcp.server\"\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:152: trailing whitespace.\n+```\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:153: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:154: trailing whitespace.\n+## More detail\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:155: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:156: trailing whitespace.\n+- [Architecture and state ownership](docs/architecture.md)\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:157: trailing whitespace.\n+- [MCP client contract](docs/client-contract.md)\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:158: trailing whitespace.\n+- [Plan-tool contract](docs/plan-tool-contract.md)\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:159: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:160: trailing whitespace.\n+## Runtime guarantees\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:161: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:162: trailing whitespace.\n+`InMemorySessionStore` is the process-local session implementation; durable reports are\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:163: trailing whitespace.\n+evidence only and cannot restore live authority. The MCP server is provider-neutral over stdio.\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:164: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:165: trailing whitespace.\n+For project build dependencies, the client inspects the project's own metadata and available host\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:166: trailing whitespace.\n+resources, prefers a compatible existing SDK/toolchain/library, and uses the project's ordinary\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:167: trailing whitespace.\n+installation or network acquisition path when none is usable. The server does not prescribe vendor\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:168: trailing whitespace.\n+locations, select a provider, or manage a build-environment fallback. Device-support packs used as\r\nSERVER_GUIDE.md:169: trailing whitespace.\n+debug authority follow the separate verified-pack onboarding contract.\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:1: trailing whitespace.\n+# Trusted CMSIS-Pack Admission\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:2: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:3: trailing whitespace.\n+Status: proposed\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:4: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:5: trailing whitespace.\n+## Summary\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:6: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:7: trailing whitespace.\n+The server must accept structurally valid CMSIS-Packs returned by the compliant setup agent\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:8: trailing whitespace.\n+without applying arbitrary archive-size, expanded-size, member-count, or compression-ratio\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:9: trailing whitespace.\n+security ceilings. Pack integrity, exact-device resolution, flash-authority derivation, and live\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:10: trailing whitespace.\n+attachment remain mandatory.\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:11: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:12: trailing whitespace.\n+This change fixes current STM32U5 onboarding. The official\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:13: trailing whitespace.\n+`Keil.STM32U5xx_DFP.3.2.0.pack` is only 8,821,594 bytes on disk, but its members total\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:14: trailing whitespace.\n+174,140,971 uncompressed bytes. The former 128 MiB expanded-size ceiling was removed, so it no\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:15: trailing whitespace.\n+longer rejects a normal official pack before the server examines its PDSC device or flash algorithm.\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:16: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:17: trailing whitespace.\n+Known regression artifact:\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:18: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:19: trailing whitespace.\n+- pack ID: `Keil.STM32U5xx_DFP`\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:20: trailing whitespace.\n+- version: `3.2.0`\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:21: trailing whitespace.\n+- source: `https://www.keil.com/pack/Keil.STM32U5xx_DFP.3.2.0.pack`\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:22: trailing whitespace.\n+- SHA-256: `e320687fe534f2fe6902e9bcdee981315abea26c4ca547142af9b9439e958be6`\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:23: trailing whitespace.\n+- archive members: 401\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:24: trailing whitespace.\n+- total declared uncompressed size: 174,140,971 bytes\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:25: trailing whitespace.\n+- maximum individual-member compression ratio: approximately 43.96:1\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:26: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:27: trailing whitespace.\n+## Trust model\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:28: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:29: trailing whitespace.\n+The setup caller is a compliant agent. It researches an official vendor pack, acquires it, and\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:30: trailing whitespace.\n+submits the exact source record and local bytes requested by the server. The pack is not an\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:31: trailing whitespace.\n+anonymous hostile upload endpoint.\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:32: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:33: trailing whitespace.\n+The server remains responsible for proving that the returned bytes can establish deterministic\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:34: trailing whitespace.\n+device authority. Trusting the agent to return the researched artifact does not allow the agent to\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:35: trailing whitespace.\n+choose memory ranges, flash sectors, a PDSC leaf, or the final pyOCD target.\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:36: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:37: trailing whitespace.\n+Consequently, archive resource ceilings are not part of the authorization boundary. They must not\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:38: trailing whitespace.\n+turn a valid official pack into an unsupported device. Structural parsing and authority checks\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:39: trailing whitespace.\n+remain part of the boundary.\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:40: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:41: trailing whitespace.\n+## Required behavior\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:42: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:43: trailing whitespace.\n+### Pack byte loading\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:44: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:45: trailing whitespace.\n+Replace the current size-bounded byte loader with a pack byte loader that:\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:46: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:47: trailing whitespace.\n+1. requires a regular, non-empty file;\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:48: trailing whitespace.\n+2. reads the selected file exactly;\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:49: trailing whitespace.\n+3. detects a file that changes while it is being read;\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:50: trailing whitespace.\n+4. computes and persists the SHA-256 of the exact bytes; and\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:51: trailing whitespace.\n+5. applies no fixed maximum archive-byte size.\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:52: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:53: trailing whitespace.\n+The existing `MAX_CMSIS_PACK_ARCHIVE_BYTES` rejection must be removed. If the\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:54: trailing whitespace.\n+`read_bounded_pack_bytes` name is retained temporarily for compatibility, its docstring must no\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:55: trailing whitespace.\n+longer claim a fixed byte bound. Prefer renaming it to `read_pack_bytes` and updating all internal\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:56: trailing whitespace.\n+call sites in one change.\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:57: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:58: trailing whitespace.\n+### Archive validation\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:59: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:60: trailing whitespace.\n+Remove these admission policies from `setup_flow/device_support.py`:\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:61: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:62: trailing whitespace.\n+- `_MAX_PACK_MEMBERS`;\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:63: trailing whitespace.\n+- `_MAX_PACK_UNCOMPRESSED_BYTES`;\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:64: trailing whitespace.\n+- `_MAX_PACK_COMPRESSION_RATIO`;\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:65: trailing whitespace.\n+- rejection based only on member count;\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:66: trailing whitespace.\n+- rejection based only on total declared expanded size; and\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:67: trailing whitespace.\n+- rejection based only on a member's compression ratio.\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:68: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:69: trailing whitespace.\n+Continue to require:\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:70: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:71: trailing whitespace.\n+- a readable ZIP archive;\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:72: trailing whitespace.\n+- exactly one parseable PDSC document; and\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:73: trailing whitespace.\n+- successful parsing by pyOCD's `CmsisPack` implementation.\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:74: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:75: trailing whitespace.\n+Those checks establish a usable, deterministic format. They are not resource limits and must not\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:76: trailing whitespace.\n+be relaxed by a caller flag.\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:77: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:78: trailing whitespace.\n+Archive member count, declared expanded bytes, and maximum compression ratio may be recorded as\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:79: trailing whitespace.\n+diagnostics. Diagnostic values must never grant authority and must not reject the candidate.\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:80: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:81: trailing whitespace.\n+### Authority checks retained unchanged\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:82: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:83: trailing whitespace.\n+The change must not bypass or weaken any of the following:\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:84: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:85: trailing whitespace.\n+- exact MCU ordering-code normalization;\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:86: trailing whitespace.\n+- exactly one matching PDSC device leaf, including the existing lowercase `x` placeholder rules;\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:87: trailing whitespace.\n+- server-derived canonical pyOCD target name;\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:88: trailing whitespace.\n+- exact pack-byte SHA-256 persistence and replay;\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:89: trailing whitespace.\n+- manifest conflict and multiple-provider rejection;\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:90: trailing whitespace.\n+- physical flash and writable RAM discovery;\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:91: trailing whitespace.\n+- unambiguous programmable/default/boot flash selection;\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:92: trailing whitespace.\n+- complete sector coverage;\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:93: trailing whitespace.\n+- usable `EraseSector` and `ProgramPage` FLM symbols, or the existing equivalent pyOCD flash\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:94: trailing whitespace.\n+  information route;\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:95: trailing whitespace.\n+- valid erased-byte value;\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:96: trailing whitespace.\n+- live target attachment before profile commit; and\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:97: trailing whitespace.\n+- later replay of the persisted pack, device, target, geometry, and identity authority.\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:98: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:99: trailing whitespace.\n+The server must continue to fail closed for missing or ambiguous device authority even though it\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:100: trailing whitespace.\n+no longer rejects a pack merely for being large.\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:101: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:102: trailing whitespace.\n+## Code changes\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:103: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:104: trailing whitespace.\n+### `src/pyocd_debug_mcp/pack_provision.py`\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:105: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:106: trailing whitespace.\n+- Remove `MAX_CMSIS_PACK_ARCHIVE_BYTES`.\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:107: trailing whitespace.\n+- Rename `read_bounded_pack_bytes` to `read_pack_bytes`, or change its contract and migrate the\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:108: trailing whitespace.\n+  misleading name in the same release.\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:109: trailing whitespace.\n+- Preserve the non-empty, regular-file, stable-read, and exact-byte behavior.\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:110: trailing whitespace.\n+- Update callers in pack provisioning, target enumeration, setup promotion, device support, and\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:111: trailing whitespace.\n+  the pyOCD adapter.\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:112: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:113: trailing whitespace.\n+### `src/pyocd_debug_mcp/setup_flow/device_support.py`\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:114: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:115: trailing whitespace.\n+- Remove the three resource-ceiling constants and their rejection branches.\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:116: trailing whitespace.\n+- Retain structural ZIP and PDSC validation.\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:117: trailing whitespace.\n+- Optionally return an immutable archive-inventory record for setup diagnostics; do not persist it\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:118: trailing whitespace.\n+  as authority.\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:119: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:120: trailing whitespace.\n+### Setup reporting and documentation\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:121: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:122: trailing whitespace.\n+- Replace wording that describes agent-returned packs as untrusted or archive-bounded.\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:123: trailing whitespace.\n+- Describe pack admission as structurally validated, digest-bound, exact-device resolved, and\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:124: trailing whitespace.\n+  live-tested.\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:125: trailing whitespace.\n+- If archive metrics are reported, label them informational.\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:126: trailing whitespace.\n+- Do not introduce a U5 family whitelist or a U5-specific exception.\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:127: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:128: trailing whitespace.\n+## Tests\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:129: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:130: trailing whitespace.\n+Add focused tests in a new pack-admission test module.\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:131: trailing whitespace.\n+\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:132: trailing whitespace.\n+1. A structurally valid pack whose declared expanded total exceeds 128 MiB is not rejected for\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:133: trailing whitespace.\n+   size.\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.md:134: trailing whitespace.\n+2. A structurally valid pack with more than 4,096 members is not rejected for member count.\r\ndocs/Live_Edit_Docs/trusted-cmsis-pack-admission-spec.